#!/bin/bash
set -eo pipefail

# Runs once, during `kamal setup`, right after docker has been installed on
# the server. There is nothing to install on top of it -- postgres arrives as
# an accessory and kamal creates its data directory itself -- so this prints
# the steps that setup does not do for you, in the order they have to happen.
domain=$(ruby -rerb -ryaml -e 'puts YAML.load(ERB.new(File.read("config/deploy.yml"), trim_mode: "-").result).dig("proxy", "host").to_s' 2>/dev/null || true)

cat <<NOTE

carscraper, first time on this server. What setup does not do:

  1. An A record for ${domain:-your domain} pointing at this server.
     Without it kamal-proxy cannot get a certificate. pre-connect refuses to
     deploy until it resolves, so you will not get far without noticing.

  2. The database starts empty, so nothing is in the graph. Either let it
     fill itself:

       bin/kamal scrape

     or carry a database you already have over an ssh tunnel to the accessory
     -- README.md, "Moving a database you already have", has that written out,
     including the postcodes, which are the slow part of a fresh start.

  3. Tell it what to look for, or a scrape finds nothing:

       bin/kamal console
       Model.create(make: "Volkswagen", model: "ID-Buzz")

NOTE
